# Guards the case where this directory is used as a Docker build context.
#
# In practice the build runs from the REPO ROOT, because pnpm-lock.yaml,
# pnpm-workspace.yaml and patches/ only exist there — see the note at the top of
# Dockerfile. Docker reads a single .dockerignore from the context root, so the
# file that governs the real build is ../../.dockerignore. This one exists so
# that a backend-scoped build cannot silently copy a local .env or node_modules
# into a layer if the context is ever changed.

node_modules
dist
coverage

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

test
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.e2e-spec.ts